<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Sept producer price index up 7.6 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African Sept producer price index up 7.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities producer price index rose 0.4 percent in September from August after rising 1.0 percent in August, Central Statistical Service figures show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in September was 7.6 percent after August's 7.4 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would rise 0.9 percent month-on-month and 8.2 percent year-on-year.  </p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Sep '96   Aug '96   Sep '95  - latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    7.6	 7.4	 7.6	  0.4	1.0</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.6	 8.5	 8.3	  0.4	1.4</p>
<p>Imported	     4.7	 4.5	 4.9	  0.1	0.1</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Sep '96   Aug '96   Sep '95</p>
<p>All commodities    108.4     108.0     100.7</p>
<p>Locally produced   109.6     109.2     100.9</p>
<p>Imported	     104.9     104.8     100.2</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
